{"id":"e052306286085efd","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-thm-functional-calculus.md","title":"Functional Calculus","display":"thm-functional-calculus — Functional Calculus","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-functional-calculus","aliases":["58-thm-functional-calculus"],"display":"thm-functional-calculus — Functional Calculus","depends_on":["[[58-df-self-adjoint]]","[[58-df-borel-function]]","[[58-df-projection-valued]]","[[58-df-bounded-operator]]","[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-functional-calculus"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-functional-calculus</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-functional-calculus — Functional Calculus"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5998e080b5d378a0\" href=\"?note=5998e080b5d378a0\" title=\"58-df-self-adjoint\">58-df-self-adjoint</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"184cdde824ccf8f9\" href=\"?note=184cdde824ccf8f9\" title=\"58-df-borel-function\">58-df-borel-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"71f1954115db03be\" href=\"?note=71f1954115db03be\" title=\"58-df-projection-valued\">58-df-projection-valued</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"2ad9c248fe18df37\" href=\"?note=2ad9c248fe18df37\" title=\"58-df-bounded-operator\">58-df-bounded-operator</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H\">\\(H\\)</span> is a complex Hilbert space and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> is a bounded operator on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H\">\\(H\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B(H)\">\\(\\mathcal B(H)\\)</span> denotes the bounded-operator algebra on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H\">\\(H\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma_H(A)\\coloneqq\\{\\lambda\\in\\mathbb C:\\neg\\exists R\\in\\mathcal B(H)\\;(R(A-\\lambda I_H)=I_H=(A-\\lambda I_H)R)\\}\">\\(\\sigma_H(A)\\coloneqq\\{\\lambda\\in\\mathbb C:\\neg\\exists R\\in\\mathcal B(H)\\;(R(A-\\lambda I_H)=I_H=(A-\\lambda I_H)R)\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_\\sigma\\coloneqq\\{O\\cap\\sigma_H(A):O\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb C}\\}\">\\(\\tau_\\sigma\\coloneqq\\{O\\cap\\sigma_H(A):O\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb C}\\}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B_\\sigma\\coloneqq\\sigma_{\\sigma_H(A)}(\\tau_\\sigma)\">\\(\\mathcal B_\\sigma\\coloneqq\\sigma_{\\sigma_H(A)}(\\tau_\\sigma)\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B_{\\mathbb C}\\coloneqq\\sigma_{\\mathbb C}(\\tau_{\\mathbb C})\">\\(\\mathcal B_{\\mathbb C}\\coloneqq\\sigma_{\\mathbb C}(\\tau_{\\mathbb C})\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B_b(\\sigma_H(A))\">\\(B_b(\\sigma_H(A))\\)</span> denotes the bounded Borel functions on the operator spectrum.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PVM}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{PVM}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoundedOperator}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{BoundedOperator}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BorelFunction}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{BorelFunction}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> are the predicates from the dependencies.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}functional\\text{-}calculus\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}operators}\\vdash\n\\mathcal B(H)\\coloneqq\\{T\\in H^H:\\mathrm{BoundedOperator}_S(T,H,H)\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}functional\\text{-}calculus\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}operators}\\vdash\n\\mathcal B(H)\\coloneqq\\{T\\in H^H:\\mathrm{BoundedOperator}_S(T,H,H)\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}functional\\text{-}calculus\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}borel}\\vdash\nB_b(\\sigma_H(A))\\coloneqq\\left\\{f\\in\\mathbb C^{\\sigma_H(A)}:\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{BorelFunction}_S(f,\\sigma_H(A),\\tau_\\sigma,\\mathcal B_\\sigma,\\mathbb C,\\tau_{\\mathbb C},\\mathcal B_{\\mathbb C})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\exists M\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall\\lambda\\in\\sigma_H(A)\\;(|f(\\lambda)|\\leq M)\n\\end{aligned}\\right\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}functional\\text{-}calculus\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}borel}\\vdash\nB_b(\\sigma_H(A))\\coloneqq\\left\\{f\\in\\mathbb C^{\\sigma_H(A)}:\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{BorelFunction}_S(f,\\sigma_H(A),\\tau_\\sigma,\\mathcal B_\\sigma,\\mathbb C,\\tau_{\\mathbb C},\\mathcal B_{\\mathbb C})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\exists M\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall\\lambda\\in\\sigma_H(A)\\;(|f(\\lambda)|\\leq M)\n\\end{aligned}\\right\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}functional\\text{-}calculus}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(A,H)\\to\n\\exists!E\\;\\left[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{PVM}_S(E,\\sigma_H(A),\\mathcal B_\\sigma,H)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land A=\\int_{\\sigma_H(A)}\\lambda\\,dE(\\lambda)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\exists!\\Phi\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Function}\\!\\left(\\Phi,B_b(\\sigma_H(A)),\\mathcal B(H)\\right)\\right.\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad{}\\land\\Phi(1)=I_H\n\\land\\forall f,g\\in B_b(\\sigma_H(A))\\;\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\bigl[\\Phi(af+bg)=a\\Phi(f)+b\\Phi(g)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\qquad{}\\land\\Phi(fg)=\\Phi(f)\\Phi(g)\\land\\Phi(\\overline f)=\\Phi(f)^*\\bigr]\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad{}\\left.\\land\\forall f\\in B_b(\\sigma_H(A))\\;\\Phi(f)=\\int_{\\sigma_H(A)}f(\\lambda)\\,dE(\\lambda)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}functional\\text{-}calculus}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(A,H)\\to\n\\exists!E\\;\\left[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{PVM}_S(E,\\sigma_H(A),\\mathcal B_\\sigma,H)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land A=\\int_{\\sigma_H(A)}\\lambda\\,dE(\\lambda)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\exists!\\Phi\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Function}\\!\\left(\\Phi,B_b(\\sigma_H(A)),\\mathcal B(H)\\right)\\right.\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad{}\\land\\Phi(1)=I_H\n\\land\\forall f,g\\in B_b(\\sigma_H(A))\\;\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\bigl[\\Phi(af+bg)=a\\Phi(f)+b\\Phi(g)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\qquad{}\\land\\Phi(fg)=\\Phi(f)\\Phi(g)\\land\\Phi(\\overline f)=\\Phi(f)^*\\bigr]\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad{}\\left.\\land\\forall f\\in B_b(\\sigma_H(A))\\;\\Phi(f)=\\int_{\\sigma_H(A)}f(\\lambda)\\,dE(\\lambda)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The spectral measure uses the four-argument PVM predicate with its carrier and Borel sigma-algebra explicit.</li>\n<li>The moment identity <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A=\\int\\lambda\\,dE(\\lambda)\">\\(A=\\int\\lambda\\,dE(\\lambda)\\)</span> ties the otherwise arbitrary PVM to the given operator and is what makes the spectral measure unique.</li>\n<li>The unital star-homomorphism laws are expanded, eliminating an undeclared placeholder predicate.</li>\n<li>The bounded Borel functional calculus takes values in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B(H)\">\\(\\mathcal B(H)\\)</span>; arbitrary unbounded Borel functions generally produce unbounded operators and cannot use this codomain.</li>\n<li>It extends polynomial calculus to continuous and bounded Borel functions.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-self-adjoint","status":"resolved","id":"5998e080b5d378a0","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-self-adjoint]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-borel-function","status":"resolved","id":"184cdde824ccf8f9","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-borel-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-projection-valued","status":"resolved","id":"71f1954115db03be","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-projection-valued]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-bounded-operator","status":"resolved","id":"2ad9c248fe18df37","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-bounded-operator]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"H","display":false},{"tex":"A","display":false},{"tex":"H","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal B(H)","display":false},{"tex":"H","display":false},{"tex":"\\sigma_H(A)\\coloneqq\\{\\lambda\\in\\mathbb C:\\neg\\exists R\\in\\mathcal B(H)\\;(R(A-\\lambda I_H)=I_H=(A-\\lambda I_H)R)\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_\\sigma\\coloneqq\\{O\\cap\\sigma_H(A):O\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb C}\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal B_\\sigma\\coloneqq\\sigma_{\\sigma_H(A)}(\\tau_\\sigma)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal B_{\\mathbb C}\\coloneqq\\sigma_{\\mathbb C}(\\tau_{\\mathbb C})","display":false},{"tex":"B_b(\\sigma_H(A))","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PVM}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BoundedOperator}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BorelFunction}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}functional\\text{-}calculus\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}operators}\\vdash\n\\mathcal B(H)\\coloneqq\\{T\\in H^H:\\mathrm{BoundedOperator}_S(T,H,H)\\}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}functional\\text{-}calculus\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}borel}\\vdash\nB_b(\\sigma_H(A))\\coloneqq\\left\\{f\\in\\mathbb C^{\\sigma_H(A)}:\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{BorelFunction}_S(f,\\sigma_H(A),\\tau_\\sigma,\\mathcal B_\\sigma,\\mathbb C,\\tau_{\\mathbb C},\\mathcal B_{\\mathbb C})\\\\\n&{}\\land\\exists M\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\forall\\lambda\\in\\sigma_H(A)\\;(|f(\\lambda)|\\leq M)\n\\end{aligned}\\right\\}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}functional\\text{-}calculus}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(A,H)\\to\n\\exists!E\\;\\left[\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{PVM}_S(E,\\sigma_H(A),\\mathcal B_\\sigma,H)\\\\\n&{}\\land A=\\int_{\\sigma_H(A)}\\lambda\\,dE(\\lambda)\\\\\n&{}\\land\\exists!\\Phi\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Function}\\!\\left(\\Phi,B_b(\\sigma_H(A)),\\mathcal B(H)\\right)\\right.\\\\\n&\\qquad{}\\land\\Phi(1)=I_H\n\\land\\forall f,g\\in B_b(\\sigma_H(A))\\;\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\bigl[\\Phi(af+bg)=a\\Phi(f)+b\\Phi(g)\\\\\n&\\qquad\\qquad{}\\land\\Phi(fg)=\\Phi(f)\\Phi(g)\\land\\Phi(\\overline f)=\\Phi(f)^*\\bigr]\\\\\n&\\qquad{}\\left.\\land\\forall f\\in B_b(\\sigma_H(A))\\;\\Phi(f)=\\int_{\\sigma_H(A)}f(\\lambda)\\,dE(\\lambda)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\\right]","display":true},{"tex":"A=\\int\\lambda\\,dE(\\lambda)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal B(H)","display":false}],"bytes":3014,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4170","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-thm-functional-calculus.md|58-thm-functional-calculus]]（batch15）"}],"outgoing":["5998e080b5d378a0","184cdde824ccf8f9","71f1954115db03be","2ad9c248fe18df37","36d7463d215be751"]}